  pmid      = {21647209},
  internal_note = {HumMod's canonical reference, added 2026-08-24 because the paper named HumMod as a third-party system with no citation anywhere in the corpus. VERIFICATION DEPTH: ABSTRACT READ at PubMed (PMID 21647209) and metadata cross-checked at Crossref (DOI 10.3389/fphys.2011.00012); the two agree on title, journal, volume 2, year 2011 and all seven author names. The article number 12 is carried by PubMed only, so that single field rests on one instrument. SEVEN authors (Hester RL, Brown AJ, Husband L, Iliescu R, Pruett D, Summers R, Coleman TG), so npj's more-than-five rule applies and the first three are listed followed by others, matching sinnige2026active. WHAT IT SUPPORTS: that HumMod is a model of integrative human physiology -- its abstract states it "consists of 5000 variables describing cardiovascular, respiratory, renal, neural, endocrine, skeletal muscle, and metabolic physiology". HARD LIMIT ON USE: this source does NOT support calling HumMod cardiopulmonary, which is far too narrow, nor lumped-parameter, which the abstract never states. Both qualifiers were removed from the manuscript on the strength of this reading. HumMod descends from Guyton's compartmental model, but that is inference and not this source's statement.}
}

