  note      = {Reference respiratory-physiology textbook. Chapter titles corrected 2026-07-27 against the 11th edition itself (Eleventh Edition, copyright 2021 Wolters Kluwer, 514 pp). Two pointers survive audit and are used in the manuscripts: Ch. 2 "Ventilation" (anatomic dead space, "The normal value is about 150 ml") and Ch. 5 "Ventilation-Perfusion Relationships" (alveolar-gas equation, on a page whose running head reads "66 CHAPTER 5"; the approximately 663 mmHg sea-level ceiling at FiO2 = 1.0 follows from it arithmetically). Three claims previously recorded here were WRONG: Ch. 4 is "Blood Flow and Metabolism", not "Blood Gas Transport" (CO2 transport is Ch. 6); Ch. 5 is not titled "Gas Exchange"; and Ch. 7 is "Mechanics of Breathing", not "Ventilation-Perfusion Relationships", so it is not where shunt is treated. Also verified: "CO2 narcosis" appears nowhere in the 9th, 10th or 11th editions, which is why the PaCO2 upper bound no longer cites this work. OPEN [2026-07-28]: the year field reads 2020, which is the publication date (13 Oct 2020 per OpenLibrary and the publisher), while the copy's copyright page reads 2021; left unchanged pending an author decision, and the same field in preprint\_npj/paper.bib carries the same note.}
